<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 16 March, from 597 BCE to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">597 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,429 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nebuchadnezzar II captures Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Babylonian Chronicle records that Nebuchadnezzar took Jerusalem, carried King Jehoiachin into exile and installed Zedekiah. A revolt led to the city's destruction in 587 BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiachin">Jehoiachin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philippines" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippines.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1521 <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Magellan's expedition reaches the Philippines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After crossing the Pacific, Ferdinand Magellan's ships sighted Samar and landed at Homonhon. Magellan was killed on Mactan in April, but one ship completed the first circumnavigation in 1522.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1660 <span class="tih-ago">366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Long Parliament dissolves itself</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">First summoned in 1640, the Long Parliament voted its own dissolution and called new elections. The Convention Parliament that followed invited Charles II to return as king.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1802 <span class="tih-ago">224 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress establishes the US Military Academy at West Point</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Jefferson signed the act founding a military academy at West Point, New York. Its graduates included Grant, Lee and Eisenhower.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1926 <span class="tih-ago">100 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Goddard launches the first liquid-fuelled rocket</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Auburn, Massachusetts, Goddard's petrol and liquid-oxygen rocket flew for 2.5 seconds and rose about 12 metres. The principle underlies most modern space launch vehicles.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1935 <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler announces German rearmament and conscription</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Defying the Treaty of Versailles, Hitler reintroduced conscription and announced an army of 36 divisions. Britain, France and Italy protested, but took no effective action.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US soldiers massacre villagers at My Lai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops killed some 350 to 500 unarmed civilians, mostly women, children and old men, in a South Vietnamese hamlet. Exposed in 1969, the massacre deepened opposition to the war.</p></div></li></ol>
